        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "E090",
          "explanation": "Provincial inspections and follow-up corrections show an active implementation discipline mechanism."
        }
      ],
      "decisive_negative_evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "E093",
          "explanation": "Late-year protest-driven COVID policy reversal indicates the system was reacting to pressure rather than smoothly executing its own line."
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "E098",
          "explanation": "IMF noted below-global-growth outlook with pandemic, property, and consumption headwinds, limiting claims of overall success."
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "E096",
          "explanation": "High R&D spending is an input, but it does not by itself prove efficient conversion into growth or innovation outcomes."
        }
      ],
      "inherited_baseline_and_constraints": "China in 2022 had very high state capacity and a closed political environment, which increases the chance of visible implementation but also of opacity and self-reporting bias. Xi also inherited severe pandemic, property, and growth constraints that limited year-end results.",
      "ruler_attribution": "Strong for elite control, agenda setting, and state-wide mobilization. Outcome attribution is mixed because many measures are system-level and the macro slowdown was partly inherited or shock-driven.",
      "supported_lenses": [
        "8B.1",
        "8B.2",
        "8B.3",
        "8B.4",
        "8B.5",
        "8B.6",
        "8B.7",
        "8B.8",
        "8B.9",
        "8B.10"
      ],
      "missing_or_weak_lenses": [
        "8B.7 is weaker because macro outcomes were mixed and partly constrained by pandemic/property shocks.",
        "8B.8 is only moderate because adaptation is visible, but often after pressure rather than through smooth self-correction."
      ],
      "contrary_evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "E093",
          "explanation": "The late-year easing shows adaptation, but also reveals that the prior approach had become untenable."
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "E098",
          "explanation": "External assessments emphasize slowdown and structural drags, so the execution record is not uniformly positive."
        }
      ],
      "source_mix": "Official party-state materials, Reuters, Bloomberg, IMF, World Bank, and specialist reporting. Strong on elite control and implementation machinery, weaker on independently verified bottom-line outcomes.",
      "structured_prior_summary": "The priors are mixed: low accountability and moderate rule-of-law scores coexist with decent government-effectiveness priors. That fits a strong command system that can execute, but with growing macro stress.",
      "chapter_rationale": "Xi's 2022 record shows high competence in the narrow sense of a tightly controlled system: elite consolidation, disciplined policy machinery, enforcement against data fraud, and state-wide planning all advanced the regime's chosen direction. The evidence is strongest on control and mobilization, not on broad prosperity. Some major policy moves were reactive, especially the late-year COVID easing, and the macro picture was uneven by the end of the year. That keeps the score below the top tier. The chapter question is about execution, not approval of the goals: on that basis Xi looks capable and forceful, but not uniformly adaptive or outcome-maximizing across the whole portfolio.",
      "lower_anchor_rejected": "A 5.5 anchor would understate the degree of elite control, policy discipline, and implementation machinery visible in 2022.",
      "higher_anchor_rejected": "An 8.0 anchor would overstate outcome quality; the economy, pandemic management, and property sector still showed major strains.",
